c{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n2. **Identify the greatest and the least member of the set:**\n   - The set in decimal form is approximately \\(\\{0.428571, 1.333333, 1.375, 0.375\\}\\).\n   - The greatest member is \\(\\frac{11}{8} = 1.375\\).\n   - The least member is \\(\\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8} = 0.375\\).\n\n3. **Calculate the positive difference between the greatest and the least member:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{11}{8} - \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{11 - 3}{8} = \\frac{8}{8} = 1.\n   \\]\n\nThus, the positive difference between the greatest and the least member of the set is \\(\\boxed{1}\\).","id":"prealgebra:855"}
